XRF Documentation******  Fehler beim Kompilieren: "Device full" etwa in Zeile 145***Program source: Computer Language June 1986Use:	- find global/local name conflicts		- program maintenance (find non-used routines)Function: File-driven cross-referencer for C and PascalOperation:		    Indicate name of source code file and output		file name (optional, default is STDOUT)		Exception files are used for implementation-		specific info (reserved words). These tokens are		ignored. 		Format: simple list of words, any number to a line,		separated by white space, alphabetical order.		The C file is	 	C.XRF  		The Pascal file is	PAS.XRF		Flow:		- read file names, open files			load exception file using input file extension			and adding .XRF.			Open this file and scan with fscanf, store on heap			Store token pointers in array EXCEPTIONS. Last ptr is NULL		- Read input file			FILTER reduces complexity to obtain a list of tokens				flag "is_c" defines language. Non-alpha are replaced				with space		- NEXT_CHAR tokenizes and numbers lines		- NEXT_SYM parses token strings & line numbers; IS_LANG			does strcmp until null prt or -1 		- NEWSYM insertion-sorts user-defined tokens into binary tree			with linked list extension containing line numbers		- SYMPRINT traverses tree and prints the tokens and the				occurrence count		- NUMPRINT reads linked line number list and prints it				(10 numbers per line) Implementation:		MAX_DEF number of entries in exception file (200)		NAME_CHARS allowed punctuationLimitation:		Does not process include files		Field references are single tokens		 ...